{{Documentation/Header}}
{{Status Templates}}
Displays a '''HIATUS''' status badge and, in the main namespace, files the page under the matching activity category. Used on utaite and group pages that are on a temporary break. Part of the status template family — see {{T|Active}}, {{T|Inactive}} and {{T|Graduated}}.

==Syntax==
{{T|Hiatus|block=1
|v1=nocat =
|v2=groups =
}}

==Examples==
* {{T|Hiatus|_Y_=1|p1=nocat = true}}
* <code><nowiki>This utaite is under {{Hiatus}}.</nowiki></code> — badge '''and''' categorizes under [[:Category:Hiatus Utaite]]
* <code><nowiki>{{Hiatus|groups=true}}</nowiki></code> — badge and categorizes under [[:Category:Hiatus Groups]]

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>nocat</code> || – || No category || Set to <code>true</code> to show the badge '''without''' categorizing (use in docs and examples). || string || – ||
|-
| <code>groups</code> || – || Group || Set to <code>true</code> to categorize into [[:Category:Hiatus Groups]] instead of [[:Category:Hiatus Utaite]]. || string || – ||
